# Copy to .env.local (gitignored) and fill in from your Supabase project's
# Settings -> API page. Create React App only exposes variables prefixed
# REACT_APP_, and it inlines them into the bundle at build time.
#
# The anon key is *meant* to be public — it identifies the project, not the
# user, and every row it can reach is gated by row-level security. Never put the
# service_role key here: it bypasses RLS entirely and this is a browser bundle.
#
# With these unset the app still runs, signed out, against this browser's own
# localStorage — which is how the test suite runs it.

REACT_APP_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project-ref.supabase.co
REACT_APP_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-anon-public-key

# --- Server side only (the /api/assist function), never REACT_APP_ ---
#
# "Ask" in the web build is read by a hosted Claude model. The call is made by
# the serverless function in `api/`, never by the browser, so this key stays on
# the server and out of the bundle. Set these in your host's environment (e.g.
# Vercel Project Settings), not here in the client build.
#
# The function verifies the caller's Supabase session (reusing the two vars
# above), so it is never an open proxy. Without a key set, the web assistant
# reports it isn't set up and nothing is sent.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY  — an Anthropic key, OR AI_GATEWAY_API_KEY to route through
#                      Vercel AI Gateway. One of the two is required.
# ASSIST_MODEL       — optional; defaults to claude-haiku-4-5.
# ASSIST_API_BASE    — optional; defaults to https://api.anthropic.com. Point it
#                      at a gateway that speaks the Anthropic Messages API.
#
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# ASSIST_MODEL=claude-haiku-4-5
